Dahl returned to the diamond on July 6, starting a six-game stint with the Boise Hawks of the Single-A Northwest League before returning to Double-A New Britain on July 17. In 72 games with the Rock Cats, he hit. 278 with 46 runs, 16 doubles, three triples, six home runs and 22 stolen bases.
Dahl said he had put the injury behind him.
"I think there was one incident during the season when I came back," Dahl said. "There was another kind of flyball like that, and I was running in and I kind of had a little flashback moment, so I kind of stopped. Thankfully, Jordan Patterson was there; right fielder came in and caught it. But that was the only time, I think. Now it's all good. There's no problem with it."
Patterson is a former standout at Baker High School in Mobile and South Alabama who also is in the Rockies' big league camp.
